    <h2>Vision</h2>
    <p>Reaching out to Makerere University Students with the gospel of Christ to impact and transform the society holistically.</p>

    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>To proclaim the lordship of Jesus Christ among students through Bible-based teaching, discipleship, prayer, fellowship, and evangelism, enabling them to grow in the Christian faith, character and service.</p>
    <img class="feature-image" src="/img/mission-community.jpg" alt="MAK CU members ministering in a local community">

    <h2>Motto</h2>
    <p><em>Preaching Christ and ministering God's Love on campus and beyond</em></p>

    <h2>Our Core Values</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Unity and teamwork</li>
        <li>Accountability and integrity</li>
        <li>Bible centered</li>
        <li>Love</li>
        <li>Servant leadership</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>History & Legacy</h2>
    <p>The Christian Union at Makerere was formed in 1962 and has been active on campus ever since. It's historically significant because it helped spark the wider Fellowship of Christian Unions (FOCUS) Uganda movement that supports similar Christian groups across universities and other tertiary institutions in Uganda. The CU has nurtured prominent national figures in the marketplace and in the body of Christ.</p>
    <p>The Christian Union has celebrated major anniversaries like 50th and 60th years, marking decades of ministry and student impact.</p>

    <h2>Who We Are</h2>
    <p>Makerere University Christian Union is a well-established Christian student fellowship operating at Makerere University in Kampala, Uganda. It's one of the oldest and most active student Christian groups in the country. The Christian Union unites all Christian students at campus, made up of currently 26 fellowships for students from colleges, Halls of residence, Hostels, and gospel mission teams.</p>
    <p>The Makerere University Christian Union is a student-led body of Christian students from different evangelical denominations who come together to worship, study the Bible, pray, and share the Christian faith on campus.</p>

    <h2>Our Structure</h2>
    <p>MAK CU is made up of fellowships across halls of residence, colleges, hostels, and mission teams, each meeting regularly to reach students where they are.</p>
